# Empty state UI

## Required component

Use a shared `EmptyState` (`src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx`) for empty lists, failed soft-empty data, and filter “no matches” messages.

Do **not** invent one-off `<p className="…-empty">` blocks for the same pattern.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<p className="browse-empty" role="status">{copy.empty}</p>

// ✅ GOOD
<EmptyState>{copy.empty}</EmptyState>
```

## Copy

- Pass message text from `UiText` (or a prop already fed by `UiText`).
- Do not hardcode empty-state strings in the component.

## Styling

- Default look is a shared class in `globals.css` (e.g. `.ui-empty`).
- Use `className` only for layout context (e.g. denser dropdown padding), not a parallel empty-message system.
- Keep `role="status"` (built into `EmptyState`) so assistive tech announces updates.
